"""Compact human report; full inventories remain linked machine-readable files."""
from .common import *
import shutil

def render(state,reason):
 pre=read(OUT/'preflight.json') if (OUT/'preflight.json').exists() else {};reg=read(OUT/'registration.json');cost=read(OUT/'completion.json') if (OUT/'completion.json').exists() else {};forecast=read(OUT/'forecast.json') if (OUT/'forecast.json').exists() else None
 text='# Belief-conditioned policy-correction PPO pilot\n\nState: **'+state+'**. Updated '+iso()+'.\n\n'+reason+'\n\n'
 text+='The scientific comparison is original frozen Hydrapple versus a state/action correction versus the same correction with a frozen belief-input channel. Only the corrections and detached value heads may train. No classifier training, checkpoint search, new embedding, reward change, decoder tuning, competition submission or paid model API is included. Original policy remains unchanged.\n\n'
 text+='## Frozen components and design\n\nThe policy is the trained embedding-final Unown Hydrapple from submission **57834515**, resolved through the playability manifest and verified by tensor hash. It is not the D10/D04 initialization or step-7,912 model. The classifier is the population-sampling MLP, **seed 11, update 14,004**. Its weights, observer, feature rules and 37-list prior are frozen. Exact hashes are in [frozen components](../experiments/'+RUN+'/frozen-components.json) and [readiness source manifest](../experiments/'+RUN+'/readiness-source-manifest.json). Private weights and rollouts stay outside Git.\n\n'
 text+='The learner keeps the original Hydrapple deck. Opponents use the unchanged current policy with conditional argmax on all **30 passing lists**, sampled by their top-100 frequency normalized over 82. These are local policy/deck packages, not the leaderboard authors’ agents. The classifier retains all 37 lists and the full prior; opponent identities from the scheduler are never inputs. Both training arms share a frozen shuffled schedule with paired chooser assignments and independent native deals.\n\n'
 text+='Actor correction: detached state384 + detached candidate256 + belief projection128 feed a shared768→256→1 GELU scorer added inside the existing conditional action procedure. Final scalar weights/bias start at zero. Legal masks, candidate order, conditional prefixes, sampling probabilities and sample-T1/argmax behavior are preserved. Critic: detached state384 + independent belief projection128 feed512→256→1, added to the existing detached384→256→1 value head. Critic gradients cannot enter the actor or frozen backbone.\n\n'
 text+='| Trainable component | Parameters |\n|---|---:|\n| Actor correction and projection | 386,561 |\n| New critic and independent projection | 321,025 |\n| Existing value head | 98,817 |\n| **Total** | **806,403** |\n\n'
 text+='The 1,479-value belief vector contains 37 deck probabilities; 143 card identities ×3 hidden zones × presence/mean/variance; 143 legally known hand counts; 3 public zone sizes; and 9 uncertainty summaries. Means/counts use fixed library maximum-copy scaling, variances its square, sizes H/60,D/60,P/6. Known hand is separate from unknown hand. State-only receives an identically sized zero vector. No hidden truth, future history or arena identity enters either actor or critic. The complete input-channel comparison does not isolate the MLP from its legal-history features.\n\n'
 text+='PPO target: 250,000 fresh decisions per arm, maximum 2,048 attempted BO3, complete 16-match cohorts with 8/8 chooser allocation. Four passes, logical 128 and actual remainder, eager bucket64/revised concurrent16, gamma 1, lambda 0.95, clip 0.2, entropy 0.01, value coefficient 2, gradient clip 1.5, per-game rewards +1/−1/0. AdamW betas(.95,.999), epsilon1e−8, decay0, foreachFalse. New branches use cosine 1e−4→1e−5 by fresh decisions; existing value head stays 1e−5. Pre-KL 0.02 stops only the cohort; post-KL 0.03 restores complete model/optimizer/RNG. No base-policy KL penalty. Collection probabilities, values, targets and belief vectors are immutable.\n\n'
 text+='## Readiness evidence\n\nSoftware preflight passed on 717 retained validation callbacks, including 48 forced callbacks and 240 selected feature points. Streaming global/local features, A allocations, legal bounds, deck probabilities, known-hand counts and zone sizes match the offline feature implementation exactly. Zero correction produces identical probabilities/actions on retained software packets. Actor/critic gradient isolation, frozen tensor identity, actual bucket64 reference, accepted disposable update, export/reload parity and forced complete rollback passed. These are software diagnostics, not strength evidence.\n\n'
 text+='Focused pytest: **9 passed** after adding worker actor-construction coverage. Earlier numerical entropy and actor-source indentation failures are preserved in [development failures](../experiments/'+RUN+'/readiness-development-failures). The indentation failure consumed one scheduled readiness intent before a native game started; it is not replaced. A separate clock-setting startup failure consumed no new native intent. Readiness uses only the remaining scheduled IDs. No readiness-updated weights or experience can become pilot training.\n\n'
 text+='| Arm | Completed BO3 | Decisions | Collection wall s | Pool startup s | Update workload s | Effective passes |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'
 for arm in ('state','belief'):
  p=OUT/f'readiness-{arm}.json'
  if not p.exists():continue
  x=read(p);text+=f"| {arm} | {x['completed_BO3']} | {x['fresh_readiness_decisions']} | {x['collection_wall_seconds']:.2f} | {x['pool_startup_seconds']:.2f} | {x['update_wall_seconds']:.2f} | {x['effective_passes']:.3f} |\n"
 text+='\nNative readiness uses one active environment plus centralized inference, with no more than four local compute threads. Worker startup, collection, serialization, observer/A/MLP work and a representative production update workload are retained separately. Native legal-action, starting-order, chooser, per-game reset and fixed-policy checks run before accepting a cohort. Conditional selection produces decision rows; forced callbacks update legal state without fabricating trainable choices.\n\n'
 if forecast:
  text+='## Budget admission forecast\n\nThe rule was frozen before belief-readiness results. It uses the existing complete GPU bucket64 cycle 103.47s/2,830 decisions, adds measured live belief CPU/4 conservatively, reserves 600s for startup/export and applies 10% timing margin. It also reserves a complete cohort beyond the target. It credits no unmeasured speedup from freezing the backbone. This is an admission estimate using prior GPU evidence, not a measured GPU result for this new correction; CPU and GPU components can overlap. Failing this forecast does not prove that optimization or a separately budgeted study cannot fit.\n\n'
  text+='| Arm | Projected BO3 with reserve | Projected GPU-session h | Cap h | Fits |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n'
  for arm,x in forecast['arms'].items():text+=f"| {arm} | {x['projected_attempts_with_overshoot']} | {x['conservative_GPU_session_seconds']/3600:.3f} | 3 | {x['GPU_fits'] and x['attempt_cap_fits']} |\n"
  text+=f"\nConservative local CPU forecast including fixed evaluation: {forecast['conservative_local_CPU_seconds']/3600:.3f} core-hours against 12. The estimate extrapolates representative mechanics and uncertain native lengths, so its limitations remain explicit in [forecast](../experiments/{RUN}/forecast.json).\n\n"
 text+='## Training and fixed evaluation\n\nActual pilot training has not started; no final correction candidate exists. Readiness updates are disposable and ineligible for selection. The registered final evaluation is1,440 fresh attempts: 3 agents × 30 lists × 16, eight per chooser. Deployment decoder is conditional argmax; population-weighted deck/chooser whole-match bootstrap and nondegenerate Wilson/MOVER envelope are frozen. No fresh strength matches or intermediate checkpoint contest have been run. If the pilot is stopped at readiness, there is no estimated strength effect, no accepted learning endpoint, and no inference that belief inputs cannot help.\n\n'
 text+='## Costs and lifecycle\n\nHard limits remain 3 GPU-session hours per arm/6 total, 12 allocated-device hours, 12 local CPU-core hours, 36 UTC elapsed hours and four local compute threads. No uploads or GPU sessions have occurred. Preparation includes a conservative 1,200 CPU-second charge; startup-repair carry is recorded separately rather than described as measured preparation.\n\n'
 if cost:text+=f"Accounted CPU: {cost['CPU_seconds']/3600:.4f} core-hours; elapsed since registration: {cost['elapsed_seconds']/3600:.3f}h. Native readiness intents: {cost['native_attempts']}; completed matches: {cost['completed_BO3']}; consumed failures: {cost['failed_attempts']}. Pilot decisions, evaluation attempts, GPU-session and allocated-device hours, uploads and paid API calls:0.\n\n"
 text+='The persistent ordinary runner saves PID, journal/logs, cohorts and failure records without model calls. No automatic follow-up is authorized. Registration, exact schedules and architecture inventory are in [experiment directory](../experiments/'+RUN+'); private checkpoints and legal observations remain in the corresponding private directory.\n'
 REPORT.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);REPORT.write_text(text)
 status=R/'docs/STATUS.md';old=status.read_text();begin='<!-- BELIEF-CORRECTION-PILOT -->';end='<!-- BELIEF-CORRECTION-PILOT-END -->';block=begin+'\n## Belief-conditioned policy correction pilot\n\n'+iso()+': **'+state+'**. '+reason+' [Report](../reports/'+REPORT.name+'). Original policy57834515 and classifier seed 11/update 14004 frozen. No automatic follow-up.\n'+end+'\n'
 if begin in old:old=old[:old.index(begin)]+old[old.index(end)+len(end):].lstrip('\n')
 status.write_text(block+'\n'+old)
 mirror=Path('/path/to/ptcg-agent')
 for p in (REPORT,status):
  target=mirror/p.relative_to(R);target.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);shutil.copy2(p,target)
 dest=mirror/'experiments'/RUN;dest.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
 for p in OUT.glob('*.json'):shutil.copy2(p,dest/p.name)
